      "dom_id": "question-85150",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "A writer is editing the first draft of a book. On average, there have been $4$ typos per page. What is the probability of finding $2$ typos on the next page? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places. You may assume that typos occur independently and at a constant average rate.",
      "worked_solution": "A Poisson random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{\\lambda }^{x}{e}^{-\\lambda }}{x!}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the number of typos on a page of the book. Since the average rate is $4$ typos per page, and events occur independently and at a constant average rate, the number of typos can be modeled as a Poisson random variable with rate $\\lambda =4,$ and we can write $X∼\\text{Po}(4).$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{4}^{x}{e}^{-4}}{x!}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability of finding $2$ typos on the next page is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=2) & =f(2) \\\\  & =\\frac{{4}^{2}{e}^{-4}}{2!} \\\\  & ≈0.147\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.",
